==Battleground==
*8 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns after 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>.
*2 [[M. Ost]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The stage has a difficult startoff due to the short delay between the Gory Dark spawns, the presence of two M. Osts and finally a Le'noir. Fighting them is actually rather straightforward, but the immense pressure from the Gory Darks and M. Ost's abilities can easily cause a loss. If you aren't careful with Le'noir, he could push easily as well, even on his own.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]: Slapsticks are Strong Against Relics and can weaken them through Talents. As stackable midranger specialists, they can easily exploit M. Ost's slow and knockback abilities to keep themselves out of range, while accumulating DPS as you send meatshields to take the heat. Ideally, they should survive until the second M. Ost and Gory Darks are gone, leaving only an unsupported Le'noir that's easier to deal with.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza Cat's massive damage to Darks makes it an excellent option to defeat the first few Gory Darks, and with Talents, its occasional Waves can potentially hit M. Ost or Le'noir to chip them. Unfortunately, its low range makes it vulnerable to curse, so it should only be spawned when the Gory Darks are dangerously close.
*[[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault CAT]] (talented): Can be used to chip down the Le'noir when it's alone, and could serve as a 4-crown alternative to Pizza.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Bomber is useful either at the beginning or the end, either to deal with the starting Gory Darks, or to permafreeze the lone Le'noir.
*[[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]: In her TF, she can not only weaken the M. Osts, but also chip the Le'noir.

==='''Reccomended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Scourge]]: Her surge can knockback the M. Osts and the Le'noir up to three times, allowing for you to regain ground easily.

==Trivia==
*No Hope Ranch's Japanese name, N.G. Ranch, is a reference to the O.K. Corral and the [[wikipedia:Gunfight at the O.K. Corral|gunfight]] that occurred there in 1881. N.G. is an acronym which stands for "No Good", the opposite of O.K.

